ezza: 8:30-13:00 e 14:45-15:45. Semifestivi: 8:30-12:00 (tutti i servizi)."},{"n":"Punta Santa Teresa Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.081095,"lo":9.88121,"d":5037,"ds":"Punta Santa Teresa Lighthouse (Italian: Faro di Punta Santa Teresa) is an active lighthouse located at the east side, opposite to the outer breakwater of the gulf of La Spezia, in the municipality of Lerici, Liguria on the Ligurian Sea.","wpu":"Punta Santa Teresa Lighthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Il_Faro_1.jpg/960px-Il_Faro_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cinque Terre National Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.1,"lo":9.75,"d":6077,"ds":"Cinque Terre National Park (Italian: Parco Nazionale delle Cinque Terre) is a protected area inducted as an Italian national park in 1999. Located in the province of La Spezia, Liguria, northern Italy, it is the smallest national park in Italy at 4,300 acres, but also the densest with 5,000 permanent inhabitants among the five towns.","wpu":"Cinque Terre National Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Manarola_NW_Cemetery_Corniglia_Monterosso_Cinque_Terre_Sep23_A7C_06872.jpg/960px-Manarola_NW_Cemetery_Corniglia_Monterosso_Cinque_Terre_Sep23_A7C_06872.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"San Pietro, Porto Venere","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.048333,"lo":9.8325,"d":6100,"ds":"San Pietro (\"St. Peter\") is a Roman Catholic church in Porto Venere, province of La Spezia, northern Italy, facing the Gulf of Poets. The Church was built upon an ancient Pagan Temple.","wpu":"San Pietro, Porto Venere","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Porto_Venere_San_Pietro_0154.jpg/960px-Porto_Venere_San_Pietro_0154.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Scoglio Torre della Scuola Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.051681,"lo":9.85856,"d":6271,"ds":"Scoglio Torre della Scuola Lighthouse (Italian: Torre della Scuola) is an active lighthouse located 243 metres (797 ft) from the north-eastern tip of Palmaria in the Gulf of La Spezia.","wpu":"Scoglio Torre della Scuola Lighthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Porto_Venere-isola_Palmaria-torre_Scola1.jpg/960px-Porto_Venere-isola_Palmaria-torre_Scola1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Palmaria (island)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.042836,"lo":9.843867,"d":6840,"ds":"Palmaria is an Italian island situated in the Ligurian Sea, at the westernmost end of the Gulf of La Spezia. With an area of 1.6 square kilometres (0.6 sq mi), it is the largest island of an archipelago of three closely spaced islands jutting from the mainland at Portovenere. The outer islands, Tino and the tiny Tinetto, lie further south.","wpu":"Palmaria (island)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Palmaria_Island_-_Porto_Venere%2C_La_Spezia%2C_Italy_-_October_25%2C_2020.jpg/960px-Palmaria_Island_-_Porto_Venere%2C_La_Spezia%2C_Italy_-_October_25%2C_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Volastra","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.1152,"lo":9.73018,"d":7769,"ds":"Volastra is one of the oldest villages in the Cinque Terre National Park, Italy. Situated above Manarola, the village is set amidst vineyards and olive groves in terraces with dry stone walls. The population is less than 200 residents.","wpu":"Volastra","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/View_South_Volastra_Cinque_Terre_Italy_Sep23_A7C_06894.jpg/960px-View_South_Volastra_Cinque_Terre_Italy_Sep23_A7C_06894.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tino (island)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.027222,"lo":9.850556,"d":8651,"ds":"Tino is an Italian island situated in the Ligurian Sea, at the westernmost end of the Gulf of La Spezia. It is part of an archipelago of three closely spaced islands jutting out south from the mainland at Portovenere. The largest of the three, Palmaria, lies to the north and the tiny Tinetto to the south.","wpu":"Tino (island)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Isola_del_Tino_-_Panorama.jpg/960px-Isola_del_Tino_-_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"San Venerio Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.026512,"lo":9.849635,"d":8712,"ds":"San Venerio Lighthouse (Italian: Faro di San Venerio) is an active lighthouse on the island of Tino, in the comune of Porto Venere in the Province of La Spezia, Liguria, Italy. Its construction began in 1839, and was completed in 1840. It illuminates and guides the sailors in that part of Ligurian Sea.","wpu":"San Venerio Lighthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Faro_dell%27isola_del_Tino-Flickr.jpg/960px-Faro_dell%27isola_del_Tino-Flickr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tinetto","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.023508,"lo":9.851264,"d":9066,"ds":"Tinetto is an Italian island situated in the Gulf of La Spezia, in the eastern part of the Ligurian Sea. It is part of an archipelago of three closely spaced islands jutting out south from the mainland at Portovenere. In 1997, the archipelago, together with Portovenere, Cinque Terre, and the Islands were designated by UNESCO as a World Heritage Site.","wpu":"Tinetto","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Tinetto.JPG/960px-Tinetto.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"The Arno is a river in the Tuscany region of Italy. It is the most important river of central Italy after the Tiber.","wpu":"Arno","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/FirenzeDec092023_01.jpg/960px-FirenzeDec092023_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}